  "result": "Perfect! Customer statements are fully implemented and working. All 163 tests pass. Here's what was added:\n\n**statement(customerId, invoices, asOf) in src/statements.js:**\n\n**Returns:** `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` or `fail('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND')`\n\n**Functionality:**\n- Filters invoices for the specified customer (normalized ID)\n- Includes only invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n- Includes only invoices with issueDate \u2264 asOf\n- Each invoice includes: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n- `due` = balance still owed (using balanceDue)\n- Sorted by issueDate ascending\n- `totalDue` = sum of all due amounts\n\n**Features:**\n- Customer ID normalization (handles case/spaces)\n- Dynamic total calculation using invoiceTotals\n- Accurate tracking of paid vs unpaid amounts\n- Excludes draft and fully paid invoices\n- Comprehensive date filtering\n\n**Example statement output:**\n```\nCustomer Statement for C-001 (as of 2025-10-31):\n\nINV-2025-0001  2025-10-07  2025-11-06  \u20ac1379.40  \u20ac689.70  (partially paid)\nINV-2025-0002  2025-10-10  2025-11-09  \u20ac2816.28  \u20ac2816.28 (unpaid)\n\nTotal Due: \u20ac3505.98\n```\n\n**Tests (12 new tests):**\n- Unknown customer error handling\n- Empty statements\n- Issued/partially_paid invoice inclusion\n- Draft and paid invoice exclusion\n- Date range filtering (before, on, after asOf)\n- Customer filtering (multiple customers)\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Customer ID normalization\n- Total due calculation\n- Mixed payment states\n\nAll 163 tests pass.",
